<title>BRAZIL: Brazil to help state on condition it privatizes.</title>
<headline>Brazil to help state on condition it privatizes.</headline>
<dateline>BRASILIA 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Brazilian government has agreed to loan Espirito Santo state 300 million reais to pay short-term debt and salaries in return for an undertaking by the state to privatize companies including its bank.</p>
<p>Espirito Santo governor Vitor Buaiz told reporters Banco do Estado de Espirito Santo would be included in the state's privatization program, along with agricultural and water and sewage companies.</p>
<p>Buaiz, who is from the left-wing Workers Party, said President Fernando Henrique Cardoso had pledged the loans would be released within a month.</p>
<p>-- William Schomberg, Brasilia newsroom 5561 2230358</p>
</text>
